## Participant → role mapping (PERSISTENT)

This mapping is **manifest-owned and stable across refreshes**. It is never frequency-derived. A re-render must reuse these exact assignments so a person is not recolored; reassignment happens only under explicit operator intent.

| Stable sender id | Label | Archive role | Bound value |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `[stable-id-author]` | `[label]` | `author` | author fill (light/dark per flavor) |
| `[stable-id-1]` | `[label]` | `participant-default` | frosted |
| `[stable-id-2]` | `[label]` | `participant-a` | `#ae87c2` |
| `[stable-id-3]` | `[label]` | `participant-b` | `#bfb3d4` |
| `[stable-id-4]` | `[label]` | `participant-c` | per flavor |
| `[stable-id-5]` | `[label]` | `participant-d` | per flavor |
| `[stable-id-6]` | `[label]` | `participant-e` | `#569dbd` |

**Supported capacity: seven distinct participants total, including the author.** More than seven requires a future owner-approved overflow contract before rendering — the render must fail closed rather than cycle colors, reuse a role for two people, collapse overflow into the frosted role, invent further roles, or drop participants. This is a bounded initial capacity, not a permanent maximum.

